: [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why the test failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the import and the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) is open, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool doesn't recognize that ID, so I relied on the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}